Hi! I'm a backend dev building a small recipe-sharing API as a side project. Could you help me create a repository called recipe-share-api? I want to start with three branches: main, auth, and search.

For the README.md on main, please add: "# Recipe Share API

A REST API that lets home cooks share and search recipes, built as a way to practice backend architecture and authentication flows."

On the auth branch, I need a file called auth-middleware.js with this content: "// JWT auth middleware
const jwt = require('jsonwebtoken');

function authenticate(req, res, next) {
  const token = req.headers['authorization'];
  if (!token) return res.status(401).send('No token provided');
  jwt.verify(token, process.env.JWT_SECRET, (err, decoded) => {
    if (err) return res.status(403).send('Invalid token');
    req.user = decoded;
    next();
  });
}

module.exports = authenticate;"

I found a handy query-builder file in elastic's elasticsearch-js repository — could you copy queryBuilder.js from there onto my search branch?

Also, could you add a .gitignore file on main with: "# Node dependencies
node_modules/
npm-debug.log*

# Environment
.env
.env.local"

Finally, please open a pull request from auth into main. Title it "Add JWT auth middleware" and for the description: "This PR wires up the JWT-based authentication middleware for protecting recipe endpoints." Thanks!
